1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,260
Think of the circulatory system as a transport system,

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:06,638
like roads and railways carrying goods around a country.

3
00:00:06,638 --> 00:00:10,432
It has three parts: the heart, the blood vessels and the blood.

4
00:00:10,432 --> 00:00:15,292
The heart is a double pump: the right side pumps deoxygenated blood to the lungs,

5
00:00:15,292 --> 00:00:19,145
and the left side pumps oxygenated blood to the rest of the body.

6
00:00:20,204 --> 00:00:26,309
Arteries carry oxygenated blood away from the heart. Veins carry deoxygenated blood back to the heart.

7
00:00:26,309 --> 00:00:28,146
Tiny capillaries connect them,

8
00:00:28,146 --> 00:00:33,066
delivering oxygen and nutrients to cells and taking away waste like carbon dioxide.

9
00:00:34,125 --> 00:00:37,800
When blood is spun in a centrifuge, it separates into layers.

10
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,763
Here are the approximate percentages of each part.

11
00:00:41,823 --> 00:00:47,276
More than half of blood is plasma, a yellow liquid. Almost all the rest is red blood cells.

12
00:00:47,276 --> 00:00:50,891
White blood cells and platelets make up only about 1 percent.

13
00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:56,751
Pause and decide: which part of the blood transports glucose and carbon dioxide,

14
00:00:56,751 --> 00:00:58,530
and which part carries oxygen?

15
00:00:59,589 --> 00:01:03,797
An adult has about five litres of blood. Spin it fast in a centrifuge,

16
00:01:03,797 --> 00:01:09,783
and it separates into layers: about 55 percent is pale yellow plasma, 41 percent is red blood cells,

17
00:01:09,783 --> 00:01:12,866
and a thin layer of white blood cells and platelets.

18
00:01:13,925 --> 00:01:15,703
Red blood cells carry oxygen.

19
00:01:15,703 --> 00:01:21,630
Their red pigment, haemoglobin, joins with oxygen in the lungs and releases it where oxygen is low.

20
00:01:21,630 --> 00:01:25,009
They have no nucleus, leaving more room for haemoglobin,

21
00:01:25,009 --> 00:01:30,995
and their biconcave disc shape gives them a large surface area to take in and release oxygen quickly.

22
00:01:32,054 --> 00:01:34,129
White blood cells defend the body.

23
00:01:34,129 --> 00:01:38,574
Some wrap around pathogens and destroy them, which is called phagocytosis.

24
00:01:38,574 --> 00:01:41,597
Others make antibodies that disable microorganisms.

25
00:01:42,656 --> 00:01:48,465
Platelets are bits of cells that help blood clot and form scabs over cuts, keeping pathogens out.

26
00:01:48,465 --> 00:01:53,681
And plasma transports blood cells, plus dissolved glucose, nutrients and carbon dioxide.

27
00:01:54,740 --> 00:02:00,904
Donating blood saves lives. We have different blood types, based partly on the antibodies in our blood.

28
00:02:00,904 --> 00:02:05,349
The main blood groups are A, B, AB and O, each either positive or negative.

29
00:02:06,409 --> 00:02:11,980
People with O negative blood are universal donors: their blood can be given safely to anyone,

30
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:14,351
so it's in high demand for emergencies.

31
00:02:14,351 --> 00:02:19,567
People with AB positive blood are universal recipients: they can receive any blood type.

32
00:02:20,626 --> 00:02:26,138
Now it is your turn to shine! Pause the video after each question and try to answer it first.

33
00:02:27,198 --> 00:02:33,006
Question 1: What type of joint is the elbow, and what movement does it allow? Pause the video now.

34
00:02:34,066 --> 00:02:37,325
Answer: A hinge joint, back and forth in one direction.

35
00:02:38,385 --> 00:02:42,830
Question 2: Why do muscles work in antagonistic pairs? Pause the video now.

36
00:02:43,889 --> 00:02:46,260
Answer: Muscles can only pull, not push.

37
00:02:47,319 --> 00:02:52,120
Question 3: Write the word equation for aerobic respiration. Pause the video now.

38
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:56,914
Answer: glucose plus oxygen leads to carbon dioxide plus water.

39
00:02:57,973 --> 00:03:02,300
Question 4: What is the function of red blood cells? Pause the video now.

40
00:03:03,359 --> 00:03:05,730
Answer: To carry oxygen around the body.
